{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Looped vertices are removed and each connected component solved alone, since the rule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composes across components. A bipartite component costs O(m √n), as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"text":", whose core pass in index order already gives the least set. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complete component takes its least vertex. Any other component of c vertices is decided","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex by vertex in index order against a witness maximum set, shrunk between decisions by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rules that keep the least set (an isolated vertex is taken; so is a simplicial vertex, such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a leaf, less than all its neighbours), with pieces that turn bipartite or complete handed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the cases above. Each decision the witness cannot answer is one solve of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"text":"‘s kind on what is left of the vertex’s component. So trees with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"few extra edges, long paths and cycles cost O(c (c + m)) at worst and O(c + m) when the rules","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"settle them, but a component the rules do not settle can cost up to c exponential searches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"far more than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"text":". Memory O(n + m + k² \/ 64) words for a kernel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component of k vertices. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()"]}],"metadata":{"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1694"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE43lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSetSay6VertexQzGyF","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"title":"Graph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","abstract":[]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","title":"Vertex","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/covering","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","title":"Covering","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"}}}